---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'June 9, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions - ScoreSpace"
  description="The terms governing your use of the ScoreSpace website, game jams, community, and published games."
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <p>
        These Terms &amp; Conditions ("Terms") govern your access to and use of the website at
        <a href="https://scorespace.net">scorespace.net</a> (the "Site"), our game jams, our
        community, and the games we publish on third-party platforms such as Discord, Reddit, and
        others (collectively, the "Services"), provided by <strong>ScoreSpace, Inc.</strong>
        ("ScoreSpace," "we," "us," or "our").
      </p>
      <p>
        By accessing or using the Services, you agree to be bound by these Terms and by our
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree,
        do not use the Services.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        You must be at least 13 years old to use the Services, and old enough to form a binding
        contract in your jurisdiction. Some platforms we publish on may impose higher age
        requirements, and you must meet those as well. By using the Services, you represent that
        you meet these requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The Services</h2>
      <p>
        ScoreSpace hosts game jams, operates a community, and publishes games that run on
        third-party platforms. We may add, change, suspend, or discontinue any part of the
        Services at any time without notice. The Services are provided for personal,
        non-commercial entertainment unless we agree otherwise in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Third-party platforms</h2>
      <p>
        Many of the Services depend on or operate within third-party platforms, including Discord,
        Reddit, and itch.io. Your use of those platforms is governed by their respective terms and
        policies, in addition to these Terms. We are not responsible for third-party platforms,
        and we do not control their availability, features, or conduct. Where these Terms conflict
        with a platform's terms as they apply to that platform, the platform's terms control for
        activity on that platform.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree that you will not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Violate any applicable law or the rights of others;</li>
        <li>Cheat, exploit bugs, use automation, or otherwise manipulate scores, leaderboards, or jam results;</li>
        <li>Harass, abuse, threaten, or harm other users;</li>
        <li>Post or transmit content that is unlawful, infringing, hateful, or obscene;</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Services or interfere with their operation;</li>
        <li>Reverse engineer, scrape, or copy the Services except as permitted by law;</li>
        <li>Impersonate ScoreSpace or any other person or entity.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may suspend or terminate your access to the Services at any time for conduct that we
        believe violates these Terms or harms other users or ScoreSpace.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Game jams</h2>
      <p>
        Participation in our game jams is subject to these Terms and any additional rules we
        publish for a specific jam. By submitting an entry, you represent that you have the rights
        to all content in your submission and that it does not infringe the rights of others. You
        retain ownership of your submission, but you grant ScoreSpace a non-exclusive, worldwide,
        royalty-free license to display, promote, stream, and feature your submission and its name,
        thumbnail, and metadata in connection with the jam and the Services. Rankings, prizes, and
        eligibility are determined at our discretion in accordance with the published jam rules.
      </p>

      <h2>6. User content</h2>
      <p>
        "User content" means anything you submit, post, or transmit through the Services,
        including jam entries, comments, ratings, and feedback. You retain ownership of your User
        content. By providing User content, you grant ScoreSpace a non-exclusive, worldwide,
        royalty-free, sublicensable license to use, host, store, reproduce, display, and
        distribute it for the purpose of operating and promoting the Services. You are solely
        responsible for your User content and the consequences of sharing it.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Services, including the ScoreSpace name, logo, text, graphics, and software (excluding
        User content and third-party materials), are owned by ScoreSpace or its licensors and are
        protected by intellectual property laws. We grant you a limited, non-exclusive,
        non-transferable, revocable license to access and use the Services for their intended
        purpose. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Virtual items and purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Some games may offer virtual items, currencies, or other purchases. Any such purchases are
        processed by the relevant platform (for example, Discord or Reddit) and are subject to
        that platform's payment terms and refund policies. Virtual items have no monetary value,
        are not redeemable for cash, and may be modified or discontinued at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        THE SERVICES ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE," WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND,
        WHETHER EXPRESS, IMPLIED, OR STATUTORY, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS
        FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT THE SERVICES WILL
        BE UNINTERRUPTED, SECURE, OR ERROR-FREE.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, SCORESPACE AND ITS OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES,
        AND AGENTS WILL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR
        PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, OR GOODWILL, ARISING OUT OF OR RELATED TO
        YOUR USE OF THE SERVICES. OUR TOTAL LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM RELATING TO THE SERVICES WILL
        NOT EXCEED ONE HUNDRED U.S. DOLLARS ($100) OR THE AMOUNT YOU PAID US IN THE PAST TWELVE
        MONTHS, WHICHEVER IS GREATER.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold harmless ScoreSpace and its officers, directors,
        employees, and agents from any claims, damages, liabilities, and expenses (including
        reasonable legal fees) arising out of your use of the Services, your User content, or your
        violation of these Terms or applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, USA, without regard to its
        conflict-of-laws rules. You agree that any dispute arising out of or relating to these
        Terms or the Services will be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and
        federal courts located in Delaware, and you consent to personal jurisdiction there.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Last updated"
        date above. Your continued use of the Services after changes take effect constitutes
        acceptance of the revised Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        We may suspend or terminate your access to the Services at any time, with or without cause
        or notice. Upon termination, the provisions of these Terms that by their nature should
        survive (including intellectual property, disclaimers, limitation of liability,
        indemnification, and governing law) will continue to apply.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms? Contact us at
        <a href="mailto:legal@scorespace.net">legal@scorespace.net</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="legal-footer-note">
        See also our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 4rem 0 3rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-bg-secondary) 0%, var(--color-bg) 100%);
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: white;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-section {
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .legal {
    max-width: 780px;
  }

  .legal p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    color: white;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .legal ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .legal li {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .legal a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .legal-footer-note {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .page-header h1 {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
